# 🎯 PUBG / PUBG Mobile: Core Gameplay & Mechanical Tips

This guide covers essential recoil management, movement tech, tactical positioning, and utility strategies to help you dominate your matches.

---

## 🔫 1. Aiming & Recoil Control

* *Vertical Recoil Compensation:* Drag down steadily on your screen (or mouse) during auto-fire sprays. For long-range engagements, rely on single-tap or 3-to-4-round bursts.
* *Gyroscope Setup (Mobile):* Enable Always On Gyroscope. Adjust your ADS sensitivity so micro-tilts handle horizontal recoil while your thumb controls vertical pull.
* *Crosshair Placement:* Always keep your reticle at head/chest height while sprinting or holding angles. Pre-aim through doors and around corners before scoping in.

---

## 🏃 2. Advanced Movement Tech

* *Peek & Fire:* Enable Lean & Open Scope in settings. Use quick left/right shoulder peeks from behind hard cover to gather info without exposing your full body.
* *Jiggle Peeking:* Move rapidly left and right while firing in close-range (CQC) hip-fire duels to disrupt your opponent's tracking.
* *Crouch-Shooting & Drop-Shotting:* Drop into a crouch instantly when opening fire to tighten your spray pattern. Drop prone (drop-shot) as a last-resort counter in open-field CQC.

---

## 🗺️ 3. Rotations & Game Sense

* *Circle Edge vs. Center Compound:* Play the edge of the Blue Zone if you prefer clearing your backline first. Hold a central high-ground compound early if you want to gatekeep rotating squads.
* *Vehicle Priority:* Always secure a Buggy or Dacia for late-game rotations. Vehicles double as mobile hard cover when popped sideways in open fields.
* *Audio Cue Tracking:* Monitor step direction, gunshots, and vehicle noise. Use mini-map sound markers to pinpoint enemy pushes before they breach your building.

---

## 💣 4. Utility Mastery

* *Smoke Grenades:* Carry at least 4–5 smokes. Use them for open-field revives, creating visual corridors during rotations, or baiting enemy fire.
* *Frag Grenades & Molotovs:* Cook frags to 1–2 seconds before throwing so enemies cannot react. Throw Molotovs onto wooden floors or behind trees to force campers out of cover.
